input.script:
export const meta = {
  name: 'design-sepclosed-chart-bridge',
  description: 'Map and design the conditional bridge: PicRankOneOpen.IsOpen -> chart family -> pic0_sepClosed_representableBy',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Map', detail: 'three readers on charts, sigma sheaf, translated cover' },
    { title: 'Design', detail: 'route synthesis' },
  ],
}

phase('Map')

const ROOT = '/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild'
const COMMON = `You are mapping Lean 4 code in ${ROOT} (Lean 4 + mathlib). READ-ONLY. Report exact declaration names, verbatim signatures, file:line. Your final message is raw data for another agent.`
const SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: { findings: { type: 'string' }, gaps: { type: 'string' } },
  required: ['findings', 'gaps'],
}

const readers = [
  {
    key: 'charts-glue',
    prompt: `${COMMON}
1. Read ${ROOT}/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/Pic0SigmaSheaf.lean IN FULL: pic0SigmaSheaf, pic0TypeFunctor, pic0RepresentableByOfCharts (line ~161) — full signatures, and what exactly a chart is (f i : yoneda.obj (X i) ⟶ (pic0SigmaSheaf C).1, hf : IsOpenImmersion.presheaf, [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective Scheme.zariskiTopology (Sigma.desc f)]).
2. Read ${ROOT}/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivRankOneOpen.lean lines 150-300: DivRankOneOpenData, divRankOneOpenData_of_picRankOneOpen_isOpen, DivRankOneOpen, divRankOneOpenMap, divRankOneOpen_isOpenImmersion — full signatures. What functor does divRankOneOpenMap map INTO, and how does that relate to pic0SigmaSheaf C?
3. How does the degree-(genus C) layer relate to the degree-0 functor pic0? grep for thetaShift / theta translation between picDegLayer (genus C) and degree 0 (ThetaShift.lean) — list the translation isos/lemmas with signatures.`,
  },
  {
    key: 'translated-cover',
    prompt: `${COMMON}
1. Read ${ROOT}/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/Pic0RankOneTranslatedCoverMembership.lean IN FULL — exists_sepClosedTranslated_mem_picRankOneOpen: full verbatim signature and docstring. What does it give exactly (for which k — [IsSepClosed k]? — which classes admit a translation into PicRankOneOpen)?
2. What is the intended use: find in the tree (grep 'translated' in Picard/, read Pic0RankOneTranslatedCover*.lean module docstrings) the design for how translated covers give JOINT SURJECTIVITY of charts onto pic0SigmaSheaf / the degree layer. Report the module docstrings verbatim.
3. Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective for zariskiTopology: what does it unfold to for a Sigma.desc of chart maps, and are there existing lemmas in the tree or mathlib establishing it from a pointwise translation statement? grep 'IsLocallySurjective' across ${ROOT}/AlgebraicJacobian.`,
  },
  {
    key: 'existing-conditional',
    prompt: `${COMMON}
Search the whole tree for existing CONDITIONAL representability assemblies: grep for 'RepresentableBy' in ${ROOT}/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/*.lean (list every declaration mentioning it with file:line + one-line context), especially anything consuming DivRankOneOpen or PicRankOneOpen.IsOpen or producing (pic0TypeFunctor C).RepresentableBy. Also read Pic0EndgameContract.lean IN FULL and report every contract statement verbatim. Also check JacobianDataQcFromRep.lean and JacobianDataFromPicRepDatum.lean for what a finished sepClosed representability must provide to continue to JacobianData.`,
  },
]

const results = await parallel(readers.map(r => () =>
  agent(r.prompt, { label: `read:${r.key}`, phase: 'Map', schema: SCHEMA, model: 'opus' })
    .then(res => ({ key: r.key, ...res }))
))

phase('Design')

const digest = results.filter(Boolean)
  .map(r => `## READER ${r.key}\n### FINDINGS\n${r.findings}\n### GAPS\n${r.gaps}`).join('\n\n')

const DESIGN_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    verdict: { type: 'string' },
    route: { type: 'string', description: 'Numbered list of Lean lemmas with precise proposed signatures and the existing lemmas each proof uses' },
    risks: { type: 'string' },
  },
  required: ['verdict', 'route', 'risks'],
}

const design = await agent(`You are designing the Lean 4 route for the AJCR Phase-6 bridge in ${ROOT}: from the conditional open-immersion data (PicRankOneOpen.IsOpen pi → DivRankOneOpenData → DivRankOneOpen with divRankOneOpen_isOpenImmersion, all landed) to the first headline milestone
  noncomputable def pic0_sepClosed_representableBy [IsSepClosed k] (h : PicRankOneOpen.IsOpen pi) (...) : Sigma fun J : Scheme => (pic0TypeFunctor C).RepresentableBy J
via pic0RepresentableByOfCharts (Pic0SigmaSheaf.lean:161), whose inputs are a family of open-immersion charts into pic0SigmaSheaf C that is jointly Zariski-locally surjective. The joint surjectivity should come from the landed translated-cover feeder exists_sepClosedTranslated_mem_picRankOneOpen plus theta-translation between the degree-(genus C) layer and degree 0. The design must respect the binding no-shortcut rules: no fieldwise statement standing in for the family-level chart, no restating goals as hypotheses; conditional on PicRankOneOpen.IsOpen is ACCEPTABLE (that is the declared route).

READER DATA:
${digest}

Deliver: verdict (is the bridge writable now, conditional on IsOpen?), a numbered route with precise signatures, and risks/what to check first.`, { label: 'design:bridge', phase: 'Design', schema: DESIGN_SCHEMA, model: 'opus', effort: 'high' })

return { design }
